1
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,039
(This story is entirely fictional)
Look.

2
00:00:11,199 --> 00:00:12,880
We won't have to sneak drinks anymore.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,000
Dad says I'm old enough to drink.

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:17,480
And look at this.

5
00:00:18,079 --> 00:00:19,440
Dad had a designer in France

6
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,359
make this for me at a hefty price.

7
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:22,120
Do you like it?

8
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,039
We'll eat it in a bit.

9
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,000
Then we'll take pictures in the garden.

10
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,159
(Based on Doctor Qin: Executer)
Mr. Zhang's guest is here.

11
00:00:33,679 --> 00:00:35,000
Take her to the west district.

12
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:41,719
But...

13
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:43,520
Xiaoxue is here

14
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,359
for Miss Xiaoya's birthday party.

15
00:00:47,679 --> 00:00:48,479
Just do it.

16
00:01:01,346 --> 00:01:05,266
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 9=

17
00:01:06,026 --> 00:01:09,140
(Public Security)

18
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,480
What are you doing?

19
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:12,359
You keep coming back.
Will you ever stop?

20
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,280
Here's the search warrant.

21
00:01:16,519 --> 00:01:17,319
(Search Warrant)
Mr. Han,

22
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:19,000
the ultra-wideband radar is ready.

23
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:20,799
One team searches inside, one outside.

24
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:21,280
Move in!

25
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:22,040
Yes, sir!

26
00:01:22,439 --> 00:01:23,640
What's this thing?

27
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:24,920
An ultra-wideband radar.

28
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,480
It can penetrate concrete and soil

29
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,799
to detect underground structures
or cavities.

30
00:01:28,799 --> 00:01:29,480
Don't worry.

31
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,599
We won't make a mess.

32
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,359
Mr. Qin.

33
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:51,000
The vegetation in the southwest corner
looks abnormal.

34
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,799
Got it.

35
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,239
Send the site data and photos
in real time.

36
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,079
Okay.

37
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:08,240
We've got a signal.

38
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,599
Mr. Han.

39
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,680
About 1.2 meters underground,

40
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,840
a 1.6-meter-long rectangular object

41
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:17,159
shows a reflection.

42
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,240
Get an excavator.

43
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,879
We've found something!

44
00:03:14,759 --> 00:03:15,560
Mr. Qin,

45
00:03:16,319 --> 00:03:18,039
we may've found buried remains.

46
00:03:18,319 --> 00:03:20,360
But based on their initial appearance,

47
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,560
they're from a canine.

48
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:22,439
A large dog.

49
00:03:22,599 --> 00:03:24,479
It's been dead for at least two years.

50
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,479
Okay.

51
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:27,759
Send me radar data
and photos of the bones.

52
00:03:28,039 --> 00:03:28,840
Take pictures.

53
00:03:31,919 --> 00:03:32,719
Come on.

54
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:35,200
(Longfan Public Security)

55
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,439
See? What did I tell you?

56
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:46,240
It's Mr. Zhang's old German Shepherd.

57
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,439
It died of old age.

58
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,599
He buried it here as a memorial.

59
00:03:49,719 --> 00:03:51,599
You made such a big fuss

60
00:03:51,599 --> 00:03:52,599
just to dig up a dog?

61
00:03:52,599 --> 00:03:53,560
What's the point?

62
00:03:53,599 --> 00:03:54,479
Officers,

63
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,719
can we call it a day now?

64
00:03:56,719 --> 00:03:58,800
Extract and label the entire skeleton.

65
00:03:59,000 --> 00:03:59,800
Ziyan,

66
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,599
keep scanning the pit.

67
00:04:00,599 --> 00:04:01,240
Yes, sir.

68
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:07,013
(Longfan Public Security)

69
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:12,919
Shiyu,

70
00:04:13,199 --> 00:04:14,439
the dog bones could be a decoy.

71
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:16,399
Dig another half to one meter down.

72
00:04:16,439 --> 00:04:17,800
Han Liang, keep digging.

73
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:20,920
Will this ever end?

74
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,040
It's all foundation rubble down there.

75
00:04:23,319 --> 00:04:25,040
(Longfan Public Security)
If you damage it, who's paying?

76
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,560
I'm calling Mr. Zhang right now.

77
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,560
I'll file a complaint against you

78
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,600
for abusing your authority!

79
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,199
Go ahead.

80
00:04:29,199 --> 00:04:30,399
Call him right now.

81
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:31,720
If you can actually reach him,

82
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:32,759
we'll stop digging.

83
00:04:32,759 --> 00:04:33,680
(Longfan Public Security)
So nervous?

84
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:35,000
Do you know what's buried down there?

85
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,879
I don't know.

86
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:37,040
(Longfan Public Security)
How would I know?

87
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,879
Mr. Han, we've found something.

88
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,920
(Longfan Public Security)

89
00:04:51,253 --> 00:04:53,053
(Longfan Public Security)

90
00:05:03,279 --> 00:05:04,759
Why can't we get through?

91
00:05:07,519 --> 00:05:08,480
Have you ever met Zhang Xiaoya,

92
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,680
Zhang Xiaodong's daughter?

93
00:05:10,519 --> 00:05:11,360
No, I haven't.

94
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,879
I've only been here for two years.

95
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,199
I heard she was sent abroad.

96
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,399
She rarely comes back.

97
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,759
I really don't know about these affairs.

98
00:05:19,279 --> 00:05:20,639
So you don't know who was buried

99
00:05:20,639 --> 00:05:21,720
in that yard, either?

100
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,199
I only knew they buried a dog.

101
00:05:23,319 --> 00:05:24,839
Who knew it'd turn out to be a person?

102
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,800
Mr. Zhang is a generous donor.

103
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,720
He'd never do something like murder.

104
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,199
Mr. Zhang has helped so many children

105
00:05:30,199 --> 00:05:31,639
who couldn't afford school.

106
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,600
If you don't believe me,

107
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:34,040
I... I have a video of him.

108
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,120
Today, we're honored

109
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:38,959
to have Mr. Zhang with us.

110
00:05:38,959 --> 00:05:40,800
He's a renowned entrepreneur
and charity donor.

111
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,879
Hello, Mr. Zhang.

112
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:42,519
Hello.

113
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:44,680
We all know

114
00:05:44,759 --> 00:05:46,439
you've always quietly done charity

115
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,800
and helped hundreds of students in need.

116
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,959
What made you

117
00:05:49,959 --> 00:05:51,879
keep doing this all these years?

118
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,240
I grew up poor,

119
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,160
so I know the importance
of helping those in need.

120
00:05:58,199 --> 00:06:00,959
I promised
to support them through school,

121
00:06:00,959 --> 00:06:03,040
from high school to college

122
00:06:03,199 --> 00:06:04,759
as long as they don't give up.

123
00:06:05,879 --> 00:06:06,680
Mr. Zhang,

124
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,399
could you say a few words

125
00:06:08,399 --> 00:06:10,079
to the children you've supported

126
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,040
on camera?

127
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:11,959
Sure.

128
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,639
This one?

129
00:06:13,639 --> 00:06:14,279
Yes.

130
00:06:18,199 --> 00:06:19,040
Kids,

131
00:06:19,759 --> 00:06:21,600
you have to study hard

132
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,480
and make your dreams come true.

133
00:06:24,279 --> 00:06:26,759
Dad will always have your backs.

134
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,600
And here are thank-you letters
from the kids.

135
00:06:38,186 --> 00:06:39,013
(To My Dear Uncle Zhang)

136
00:06:39,050 --> 00:06:39,733
(For Dear Mr. Zhang)

137
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:40,720
A kind man like him

138
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:42,800
who cares so much for the poor kids

139
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,879
would never murder someone!

140
00:06:44,879 --> 00:06:46,399
Someone must be framing him.

141
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:48,600
Or maybe it's just some old issue

142
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,240
left over from the villa's past.

143
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,040
Liang.

144
00:06:51,399 --> 00:06:52,199
What's going on?

145
00:06:52,319 --> 00:06:53,800
No record of Zhang Xiaodong
leaving the country

146
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,600
or taking public transportation.

147
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,079
Let's check the backyard again.

148
00:06:59,199 --> 00:07:00,600
(Longfan Public Security)
Shiyu, how's it going?

149
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,199
The initial assessment is,

150
00:07:02,199 --> 00:07:04,160
the victim died
more than five years ago.

151
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:06,079
Based on epiphyseal fusion

152
00:07:06,079 --> 00:07:08,680
and tooth eruption,

153
00:07:09,399 --> 00:07:10,879
the victim was likely under 20.

154
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,040
Under 20?

155
00:07:12,439 --> 00:07:13,399
Still a kid?

156
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:14,040
Yes.

157
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:16,199
Judging by the body's burial position

158
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:18,240
and the soil staining around it,

159
00:07:18,519 --> 00:07:20,040
the body was buried in a hurry.

160
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,360
There was no coffin or wrapping.

161
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:24,240
I need more tests
to determine the cause of death.

162
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:25,879
But one thing I can say for sure.

163
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,040
This was a brutal homicide.

164
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,759
The butler's only been here
for two years,

165
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:30,000
so he doesn't know much.

166
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,600
If we want to dig deeper,

167
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,639
we need someone who's been here longer.

168
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:35,160
Mr. Han.

169
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,040
We found Chen Guofu,

170
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,120
a driver who worked here for ten years.

171
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,759
He quit last year due to health issues.

172
00:07:40,759 --> 00:07:41,399
Ziyan,

173
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:43,199
look into Chen Guofu with Ou Wen.

174
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:43,959
Yes, sir.

175
00:07:43,959 --> 00:07:44,639
Let's go.

176
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,439
Mr. Chen,

177
00:07:50,639 --> 00:07:51,600
we're here today

178
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:53,680
to learn more about Zhang Xiaodong

179
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,959
and his daughter, Zhang Xiaoya.

180
00:07:57,319 --> 00:07:59,040
Miss... Miss Xiaoya?

181
00:07:59,759 --> 00:08:02,000
She's been studying abroad all along.

182
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,000
You worked for Mr. Zhang
for many years, right?

183
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,199
About ten years or so.

184
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,240
Then my eyesight started to fail.

185
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:11,040
I couldn't see well at night.

186
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:14,560
And I was too old to keep up.

187
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:16,079
How was Mr. Zhang as a boss?

188
00:08:17,399 --> 00:08:20,639
He always paid me on time.

189
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,680
He even helped
with my child's schooling.

190
00:08:24,199 --> 00:08:26,279
In that sense, he was a good boss.

191
00:08:26,439 --> 00:08:27,199
But...

192
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:31,639
There were things

193
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,759
that we drivers

194
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,720
have to turn a blind eye to.

195
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:38,679
About Miss Zhang Xiaoya,

196
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:39,720
we found problems

197
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,440
with her records of going abroad.

198
00:08:50,519 --> 00:08:53,559
Since you've dug this deep,

199
00:08:55,399 --> 00:08:56,440
some things

200
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,960
shouldn't weigh on my heart any longer.

201
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,159
I'll tell you.

202
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:07,440
I'll start with Miss Xiaoya.

203
00:09:07,759 --> 00:09:10,600
I watched that girl grow up.

204
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,639
She'd sit in the back seat
at seven or eight,

205
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:17,279
calling me "Uncle Chen" over and over,

206
00:09:17,919 --> 00:09:20,240
and always sharing her snacks with me.

207
00:09:21,559 --> 00:09:22,960
She was such a sweet girl.

208
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,600
But as she grew up

209
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,080
and started middle school,

210
00:09:31,399 --> 00:09:34,279
she hardly ever saw Mr. Zhang.

211
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,159
I usually drove her around.

212
00:09:36,519 --> 00:09:37,600
Sometimes I thought

213
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,399
she was even more pitiful
than my own child.

214
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,440
At least my child
gets to see me every day.

215
00:09:43,639 --> 00:09:44,440
But she...

216
00:09:44,679 --> 00:09:46,399
If she wanted to see her own father,

217
00:09:46,559 --> 00:09:47,879
she had to make an appointment.

218
00:09:47,879 --> 00:09:49,639
What was her relationship
with Zhang Xiaodong like?

219
00:09:49,919 --> 00:09:50,840
How should I put it?

220
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:54,000
He gave her whatever she wanted.

221
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:58,000
The best clothes, bags, and phones.

222
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:00,679
But that kind of love

223
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,360
was about giving money,

224
00:10:03,799 --> 00:10:05,200
not giving his heart.

225
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:09,679
It was sometime
before her 18th birthday.

226
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:12,360
I can't remember the exact date.

227
00:10:12,559 --> 00:10:14,399
It was in the autumn, anyway.

228
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,360
She drank a lot that day.

229
00:10:16,559 --> 00:10:18,639
Didn't you promise me

230
00:10:19,879 --> 00:10:22,879
you'd never hurt my friends?

231
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:27,840
She's my very, very best friend.

232
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,159
She said...

233
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:33,639
she'd never hang out with me again!

234
00:10:33,720 --> 00:10:35,440
She'd never speak to me again!

235
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,639
What did you do to her?

236
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,639
Did you yell at her?

237
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,759
Did you hit her?

238
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,639
Xiaoya, you're drunk.

239
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,279
All you need to know

240
00:10:53,879 --> 00:10:55,600
is everything I do

241
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,960
is to give you the best.

242
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,960
Some friends just aren't worth having.

243
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:03,080
Forget her.

244
00:11:11,559 --> 00:11:12,399
Dad...

245
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:17,440
She said our family was disgusting.

246
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,240
Why?

247
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,879
Miss Xiaoya was a very kind girl.

248
00:11:24,799 --> 00:11:28,000
She often brought classmates
to the villa.

249
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:31,600
Starting around the time she was 17,

250
00:11:32,559 --> 00:11:33,840
I gradually noticed

251
00:11:34,480 --> 00:11:36,919
that some of the girls who came over

252
00:11:36,919 --> 00:11:39,000
always seemed off when they left.

253
00:11:39,039 --> 00:11:39,840
Meng.

254
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,000
Meng.

255
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,759
Are you feeling sick?

256
00:11:48,759 --> 00:11:49,600
What's wrong?

257
00:11:51,679 --> 00:11:52,480
What's wrong?

258
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:55,360
You were fine earlier, right?

259
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,039
Miss Xiaoya even asked Mr. Zhang
about it.

260
00:11:59,519 --> 00:12:00,679
Mr. Zhang always said,

261
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,159
"Kids are like that."

262
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:03,960
"Their moods change quickly."

263
00:12:04,679 --> 00:12:06,799
Eventually, Miss Xiaoya believed him.

264
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:07,960
After that,

265
00:12:08,919 --> 00:12:11,440
she rarely brought classmates home

266
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,960
until her 18th birthday.

267
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,799
That was the last time I saw her.

268
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
That night,

269
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:20,000
the villa was packed.

270
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:21,240
There were so many people.

271
00:12:21,519 --> 00:12:22,960
When the party was almost over,

272
00:12:23,559 --> 00:12:24,360
Su Shi,

273
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:28,039
the Ms. Su I mentioned earlier,

274
00:12:28,279 --> 00:12:29,799
asked me to wait by the back door.

275
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:33,360
She said I'd drive a VIP home.

276
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,519
A VIP?

277
00:12:34,639 --> 00:12:35,440
Who?

278
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,759
I didn't know her name.

279
00:12:37,919 --> 00:12:39,039
But that girl...

280
00:12:40,159 --> 00:12:41,960
I'll never forget her.

281
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:43,680
(Do Not Pull)

282
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:54,746
(Automatic Door)

283
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:56,759
Here, take this.

284
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:05,440
Where did you take her?

285
00:13:06,759 --> 00:13:09,200
She seemed uneasy the whole ride.

286
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,120
Not long after we left,

287
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,840
she insisted on getting out.

288
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:13,879
Sir,

289
00:13:15,039 --> 00:13:15,840
stop the car.

290
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,080
I want to get out.

291
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:24,546
(Fan A 71954)

292
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:34,039
Then I went back to the villa
and returned the car.

293
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:37,000
That's when something strange happened.

294
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:38,679
Mr. Zhang suddenly said

295
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:40,600
he had family matters to deal with.

296
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:42,559
He'd give me a month of paid leave

297
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:45,039
so I could visit my family.

298
00:13:45,399 --> 00:13:46,840
Giving a month off out of nowhere?

299
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:50,200
I was actually pretty happy.

300
00:13:51,919 --> 00:13:53,200
In all those years,

301
00:13:53,639 --> 00:13:56,080
he'd never been that generous.

302
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,000
I had barely left

303
00:13:58,799 --> 00:14:01,360
when Miss Xiaoya was sent abroad.

304
00:14:01,759 --> 00:14:02,799
After you came back,

305
00:14:02,799 --> 00:14:04,840
didn't you ask about Zhang Xiaoya?

306
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,879
When I came back,

307
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,200
they told me

308
00:14:08,879 --> 00:14:10,879
Miss Xiaoya was settled abroad.

309
00:14:11,279 --> 00:14:15,240
Everything in the villa
that belonged to her

310
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:19,639
was suddenly packed away.

311
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,000
Mr. Chen,

312
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,360
thanks for today.

313
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:30,600
The information you gave us
is very important.

314
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,759
If you remember anything else,

315
00:14:32,759 --> 00:14:34,200
please contact us anytime.

316
00:14:36,519 --> 00:14:37,399
Officers,

317
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:43,000
if something really happened
to Miss Xiaoya,

318
00:14:44,639 --> 00:14:46,960
please make sure she gets justice.

319
00:14:47,919 --> 00:14:48,799
We will.

320
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,279
Here you are again.

321
00:15:03,639 --> 00:15:05,600
(Weiyou Mart)
Yeah, just passing by.

322
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,440
You look pretty tired lately.

323
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,240
(Weiyou Mart)
So I stopped by.

324
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,240
You're tired too, right?

325
00:15:14,759 --> 00:15:16,000
So we're both tired.

326
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,559
I always feel like you're testing me.

327
00:15:20,440 --> 00:15:21,799
But you never ask me outright.

328
00:15:22,759 --> 00:15:23,840
So I can't tell

329
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:26,440
if you really care about me.

330
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,039
I'm not testing you...

331
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:32,759
Qin Ming,

332
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,480
if you have questions for me,

333
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,799
just go ahead.

334
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:37,480
I'll be waiting.

335
00:15:41,919 --> 00:15:45,200
If I ever really ask you something,

336
00:15:46,759 --> 00:15:48,200
will you tell me the truth?

337
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,159
What about you?

338
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:54,000
Will you believe me?

339
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:57,173
(Weiyou Mart)

340
00:16:18,399 --> 00:16:19,600
First, an overall examination.

341
00:16:20,399 --> 00:16:22,440
No animal bite marks on the bones.

342
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:25,159
The time of death is estimated
at eight to ten years ago.

343
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,879
The bone surfaces show mild weathering,

344
00:16:26,879 --> 00:16:29,440
but the bone structure
isn't severely degraded.

345
00:16:29,919 --> 00:16:31,559
Shiyu, look at the pelvis.

346
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,639
About the pubic symphysis,

347
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,080
the pubic arch angle is over 90 degrees.

348
00:16:36,279 --> 00:16:37,759
The ischiopubic rami are slender.

349
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,759
The pelvic inlet is oval-shaped.

350
00:16:39,799 --> 00:16:40,600
Female.

351
00:16:42,559 --> 00:16:45,080
The medial clavicular epiphysis
hasn't fully fused.

352
00:16:45,279 --> 00:16:47,519
The epiphyseal line
remains visible and wavy,

353
00:16:47,879 --> 00:16:49,840
with a distinct separation
from the shaft.

354
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:52,080
The victim was no older than 20.

355
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:57,519
The third molars have erupted

356
00:16:57,799 --> 00:16:58,960
with minimal wear on the cusps.

357
00:16:58,960 --> 00:17:00,080
What's a third molar?

358
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:00,919
A wisdom tooth.

359
00:17:00,919 --> 00:17:02,440
Based on the skeletal findings,

360
00:17:02,679 --> 00:17:04,720
she was about 18 years old.

361
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,079
Only 18?

362
00:17:09,279 --> 00:17:10,079
Look here.

363
00:17:10,519 --> 00:17:12,039
The left parietal region of the skull

364
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,759
has a clear linear fracture.

365
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,880
I see it.

366
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:17,160
It extends from the parietal bone
to the temporal bone.

367
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:19,680
The fracture starts
near the parietal tuber

368
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,319
and extends anteroinferiorly,

369
00:17:21,519 --> 00:17:23,079
ending at the squamous part
of the temporal bone.

370
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,079
The edges are clean

371
00:17:25,319 --> 00:17:26,559
with no signs of healing.

372
00:17:26,680 --> 00:17:27,920
This was antemortem.

373
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:30,960
A linear fracture
caused by direct blunt force.

374
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,160
Can we identify the weapon?

375
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:34,000
On the corresponding area
of the inner skull,

376
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,680
there's a clear extension
of the fracture line,

377
00:17:36,079 --> 00:17:38,039
which means the impact was severe.

378
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:39,920
The weapon was likely

379
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,359
a blunt object with a flat surface.

380
00:17:41,519 --> 00:17:44,680
Like a table corner,
wall edge, or floor.

381
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:46,680
A skull fracture this severe,

382
00:17:46,839 --> 00:17:47,880
especially when the fracture line

383
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,799
crosses the path
of the middle meningeal artery,

384
00:17:50,359 --> 00:17:51,799
can easily rupture the artery

385
00:17:51,799 --> 00:17:53,240
and cause an epidural hematoma.

386
00:17:53,559 --> 00:17:55,759
The hematoma can rapidly expand
and compress the brain.

387
00:17:55,799 --> 00:17:56,880
Without prompt surgery,

388
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,119
death is only a matter of time.

389
00:17:58,599 --> 00:17:59,480
Now, the base of the skull.

390
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:01,440
Around the foramen magnum,

391
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,079
there are no obvious signs of fracture.

392
00:18:03,559 --> 00:18:07,640
But the right middle cranial fossa shows
slight bone plate displacement,

393
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,680
consistent with a contrecoup injury.

394
00:18:08,680 --> 00:18:11,119
This means the head
was accelerating or decelerating

395
00:18:11,559 --> 00:18:13,319
at the time of impact.

396
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,200
Impact?

397
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,279
What kind of impact?

398
00:18:15,279 --> 00:18:17,519
She may've fallen and hit her head,

399
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,240
or fallen after being struck.

400
00:18:21,079 --> 00:18:25,079
Was it an accident or homicide?

401
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:27,240
The victim was a woman around 18.

402
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,880
She died from blunt-force trauma
to the head,

403
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:31,960
causing a skull fracture
and intracranial bleeding.

404
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:34,279
She died around eight to ten years ago.

405
00:18:35,279 --> 00:18:37,519
Next, send her remains
to the police department

406
00:18:38,079 --> 00:18:39,359
for 3D craniofacial reconstruction.

407
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:40,680
Understood.

408
00:18:41,039 --> 00:18:42,519
I'll wait for her facial reconstruction

409
00:18:42,519 --> 00:18:43,680
and identify her.

410
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:49,519
These remains have been buried
for ten years.

411
00:18:50,359 --> 00:18:51,440
She's been waiting for ten years

412
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:54,119
just to tell us who she is.

413
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,920
We can't let her wait in vain.

414
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,319
I'll contact the police department now.

415
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,519
Eighteen years old.

416
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,559
Another young life cut short.

417
00:19:13,319 --> 00:19:14,079
Qin?

418
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,240
Qin, are you alright?

419
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,440
What's wrong?

420
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:57,953
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

421
00:19:58,510 --> 00:20:02,660
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

422
00:20:02,833 --> 00:20:06,510
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

423
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:11,086
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

424
00:20:20,126 --> 00:20:23,800
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

425
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:26,520
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

426
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:31,260
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

427
00:20:31,326 --> 00:20:35,080
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

428
00:20:35,406 --> 00:20:39,680
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

429
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:44,060
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

430
00:20:45,153 --> 00:20:48,340
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

431
00:20:49,113 --> 00:20:53,000
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

432
00:21:01,990 --> 00:21:05,780
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

433
00:21:06,193 --> 00:21:10,070
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

434
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:13,980
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

435
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:16,990
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

436
00:21:17,046 --> 00:21:21,710
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

437
00:21:21,980 --> 00:21:26,060
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

438
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:28,830
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

439
00:21:28,886 --> 00:21:30,630
♪We stop here in this night♪

440
00:21:30,926 --> 00:21:35,320
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

441
00:21:35,640 --> 00:21:41,113
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

442
00:21:43,966 --> 00:21:49,640
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

443
00:22:01,553 --> 00:22:04,470
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

444
00:22:04,470 --> 00:22:09,046
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

445
00:22:10,766 --> 00:22:16,420
♪One gunshot echoes♪
